     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">It works!!!<div>Thank&#39;s a lot for you help! Really, a big thanks!</div><div>Regards</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br>Em quinta-feira, 19 de maio de 2016 01:55:43 UTC+1, Yihui Xie  escreveu:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">1. rows_all should work in the server-side processing mode with the\r\n<br>development version of DT: <a href=\"https://github.com/rstudio/DT\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/rstudio/DT&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792393454021000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2GgERW8i5D60JrzZyDtpQS\">https://github.com/rstudio/DT</a>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>2. The table header issue may also have been solved in the development\r\n<br>version of DT. Please try it and let me know if it is not.\r\n<br>\r\n<br>Regards,\r\n<br>Yihui\r\n<br>\r\n<br>On Wed, May 18, 2016 at 10:59 PM, Carlos Leite\r\n<br>&lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">carlosmaga...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:\r\n<br>&gt;\r\n<br>&gt; Hi,\r\n<br>&gt;\r\n<br>&gt; I am using datatables in a shiny app.\r\n<br>&gt; If I use the server side processing:\r\n<br>&gt;\r\n<br>&gt; output$printrules &lt;- DT::renderDataTable(DT::datatable({\r\n<br>&gt; rulesp()\r\n<br>&gt; }, options = list(scrollX = TRUE, aLengthMenu = c(5, 10, 25, 50), iDisplayLength = 10)))\r\n<br>&gt;\r\n<br>&gt; It&#39;s all ok, but when I try to do input$printrules_rows_all it just prints the current rows.\r\n<br>&gt; I&#39;ve read that rows_all isn&#39;t working on the server side processing. Then I switched to the client side processing:\r\n<br>&gt;\r\n<br>&gt; output$printrules &lt;- DT::renderDataTable(DT::datatable({\r\n<br>&gt;  rulesp()\r\n<br>&gt; }, options = list(scrollX = TRUE, aLengthMenu = c(5, 10, 25, 50), iDisplayLength = 10)), server=FALSE)\r\n<br>&gt;\r\n<br>&gt;\r\n<br>&gt; (rulesp() is a reactive function that returns a dataframe)\r\n<br>&gt;\r\n<br>&gt; And I am able to get the indexes of the rows. However the table is printed in a different way. The numbers become rounded and the table, somehow, gets messy. The 1.00000 become 1. And the spaces between columns become unformatted. This happens because the size of the columns vary. How to solve this? Is there a way to get the indexes in the server side processing? If not, how can I solve this strange behaviour?\r\n<br>&gt;\r\n<br>&gt; P.S sometimes when I render a datatable, let&#39;s imagine that I put to show 10 entries, it will only show 5 and a bit unformatted. I need to change the page (NEXT) or so for the datatable to reajust.\r\n<br>&gt;\r\n<br>&gt; Thank&#39;s a lot\r\n<br>&gt;\r\n<br>&gt; Server=TRUE\r\n<br>&gt;\r\n<br>&gt;\r\n<br>&gt;\r\n<br>&gt;\r\n<br>&gt;\r\n<br>&gt;\r\n<br>&gt;\r\n<br>&gt;\r\n<br>&gt;\r\n<br>&gt; Server =FALSE\r\n<br>&gt;\r\n<br></blockquote></div></div>"
    ]
